// Plant engineering: CFIHOS 2.0 and DEXPI 2.0.1: the standards' constraints, their sample data and the links between them
//
// Generated by ../../crosswalk.py from crosswalk.json, sample.json and the model.json and sample.json of each
// standard. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// Each standard's labels and relationship types are prefixed: CFIHOS 2.0 as cfihos__, DEXPI 2.0.1 as dexpi__. The
// links between them are not.
//
// The Kestrel Gas Processing Plant as its CFIHOS handover and its DEXPI P&ID describe it, linked where the two
// describe the same thing: the operator, Kestrel Energy; the plant; its condensate stabilisation and export unit; the
// export pumps P-2001A and P-2001B; and their motors, tagged PM-2001A and PM-2001B in the handover and drawn as
// components of the pumps on the P&ID. The two samples name the site and the area differently, so they are not
// linked. CFIHOS 2.0: An engineering contractor's handover of the condensate export pumps at the fictional Kestrel
// Gas Processing Plant. Tags P-2001A/B and their motors sit in a process unit and area of the plant, classed by the
// CFIHOS reference data and fulfilled by serialised equipment of a manufacturer's model parts. The purchase order
// that bought them, the spare parts interchangeability record for their mechanical seals, and an as-built vendor data
// sheet with its revision, references and transmittal complete the handover. Codes such as the CFIHOS unique codes
// are illustrative. DEXPI 2.0.1: A P&ID extract of the fictional Kestrel Gas Processing Plant, exchanged between
// engineering tools in the DEXPI format. Condensate line 20-113 runs from the feed drum PV-2010 through export pump
// P-2001A, its discharge valve GV-2001 and flow element FE-2001 to an off-page connector. The flow control loop
// L20.001 senses the segment with an orifice measuring system, conveys the signal to controller FIC-2010 and actuates
// globe valve FV-2001 through a fail-close actuator. Duty and standby pumps, with their motors and impellers, sit in
// the plant's breakdown from enterprise to section, area, system and train.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The standards: their constraints

